# Design system

Light, bright SaaS/tool-directory. White/very-light surfaces, generous whitespace, rounded cards, subtle shadows, soft pastel accents. Purple/indigo is the brand accent. Friendly and uncluttered.

Do not redesign the app. Match this language when adding or restyling UI. Do not introduce an unrelated identity, heavy glassmorphism, or neon/dark-first themes. `next-themes` dark mode already exists — keep it working via semantic tokens; do not make dark the default.

## Tokens (do not invent a second palette)

Define/extend CSS variables in `src/app/globals.css`. Prefer Tailwind semantic classes: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `text-primary`, `bg-primary`, `border-border`, `ring-ring`.

Existing:

- Primary: `--primary` (violet/purple, ~`#7c3aed` / oklch 292°)
- Neutrals: white `--background`/`--card`; navy `--foreground`; muted body `--muted-foreground`; soft `--border`
- Radius: `--radius: 0.75rem` → `rounded-md` controls, `rounded-xl` cards, `rounded-full` pills
- Shadow: `shadow-sm` / `shadow-md`; hover `shadow-primary/10`–`/20`. No heavy dark shadows
- Font: Geist (`--font-geist-sans`) + Geist Mono. Do not add decorative fonts

Pastel accents (icon wells, chips — not raw hex sprinkled in components): lavender/purple, soft blue, mint, peach, pink/rose, light teal. Reuse `primary/10`, `indigo-500/10`, `purple-500/10`, `emerald-400/20` style washes already on the home hero.

Heading highlight: `bg-linear-to-r from-indigo-500 via-purple-500 to-pink-500 bg-clip-text text-transparent` (header, hero, tool titles). Do not put that gradient on every button/card.

Reuse existing utilities before writing new CSS: `gradient-text`, `modern-card`, `hover-lift`, `touch-target`, `p-responsive-*`, `text-responsive-*`. Prefer `Button` / `Card` / `Badge` / `Input` from `src/components/ui/`.

## Shape and cards

Rounded search fields, CTAs, category pills, icon containers. Avoid sharp rectangles.

Default discovery card: light `bg-card`, `rounded-xl`, subtle border/shadow, pastel icon well, clear title, muted description, small category/popular badge, chevron/CTA, comfortable padding. Variants allowed when hierarchy needs them.

## Motion and layout

Subtle hover lift/fade only. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Do not add animation libraries; `motion/react` is already the one.

Home (existing): spacious hero → featured tools → search + category pills → tool grid → newsletter → footer. Keep search in `ToolSearch` — do not add a second search. Header is sticky, light, backdrop-blur; footer is light with purple accent and categorized links.

Responsive: desktop multi-column; tablet fewer columns; mobile 1–2 card columns; stack search/filters; collapse nav; keep tool actions visible.

Hero atmosphere: soft indigo/purple/pink gradient orbs on a light background. Stats may use real product facts already on the page (`18+` tools, free, PWA) — never fake social proof.
